Hi there,

I have some confusion over the use of the formula option in addqtl(). I'm hoping someone can shine a light for me here.
For some reason, I assume by not providing an explicit formula to addqtl, it by default uses the qtl object (provided as input option) as an additive covariate and searches for any additional additive QTL. Basically, i'm thinking the following calls are equivalent

#We make a qtl object with one qtl
qtl1 <- makeqtl(args)
#Then the following two calls should be equivalent
addqtl(cross, qtl=qtl1, formula=y~Q1+Q2)
addqtl(cross, qtl=qtl1)

This could be an incorrect assumption but any light on this would be helpful. Specifically, I have genotypes (~8000 on 384 individuals) called using the MSG (Andolfatto et al 2011) pipeline for a Backcross. I read these into R (3.4.4) using David Sterns read.cross.msg (https://github.com/dstern/read_cross_msg/blob/master/read.cross.msg.1.5.R) function. I then perform the following in with qtl (qtl_1.42-8):

#covariates for the qtl analysis
body <- pull.pheno(eye, c("Leg2_Av", "Leg3_Av", "sex"))
#scan one eyearea.hk <http://eyearea.hk> <- scanone(eye, pheno.col=3, method="hk",addcovar=body, verbose=T) plot(eyearea.hk <http://eyearea.hk>, chr=3) #attached: scanone.png
#          chr      pos   lod
#2:39184043   2 39184043 2.310
#3:39299663   3 39299663 4.990
#4:92481      4    92481 0.885
#X:8357231    X  8357231 2.180

#then i make a qtl object with highest lod score
qtl1 <- makeqtl(eye, chr=3, pos=39299663, what="prob")
#and run addqtl without a formula to find evidence for additional additive qtl
eyearea.hk2_nf <- addqtl(eye, pheno.col = 3, qtl=qtl1, covar=body, method="hk" )
Warning message:
In addqtl(eye, pheno.col = 3, qtl = qtl1, covar = body, method = "hk") :
  Dropping 2 individuals with missing phenotypes.

plot(eyearea.hk2_nf) #attached: addqtl_Noformula.png
summary(eyearea.hk2_nf)
#           chr      pos     lod
#2:39184043   2 39184043   2.766
#3:609806     3   609806   4.270
#4:100310     4   100310   0.735
#X:8357231    X  8357231 -53.824

#and then addqtl with a formula saying that any additional qtl (Q2) is additive with Q1
eyearea.hk2_f <- addqtl(eye, pheno.col = 3, qtl=qtl1, covar=body, formula=y~Q1+Q2, method="hk" )
Warning message:
In addqtl(eye, pheno.col = 3, qtl = qtl1, covar = body, formula = y ~  :
  Dropping 1 individuals with missing phenotypes.

plot(eyearea.hk2_f)  #attached: addqtl_formula.png
summary(eyearea.hk2_f)
#          chr     pos   lod
#2:4714      2    4714 2.114
#3:2903347   3 2903347 3.318
#4:39884     4   39884 0.923
#X:8643217   X 8643217 5.265

The two runs of addqtl are quite different and I'm not sure what the highly negative LOD on the X could mean (in the run with no formula). Surely the one or two individuals dropped between the analysis could make this difference? And to be honest, I'm not sure why a different number of phenotypes are dropped between the two instances. What is addqtl doing when no formula is specified? Any input would be appreciated.

best,
Saad

